Custom firewall rules for Issabel
=================================

Files in this directory are applied by `fwconfig --load` after the Issabel
chains are created and before the normal rules are loaded.

* `*.rules`  -> IPv4, applied with `iptables-restore --noflush`
* `*.rules6` -> IPv6, applied with `ip6tables-restore --noflush`

The files are applied in alphabetical order. They must be owned by
`root:root`, must not be writable by group or others, and must not be
symlinks. `fwconfig` runs `iptables-restore --test` first and aborts the
whole load if a file is invalid.

Use the Issabel chains rather than the built-in ones:

  ISSABEL_HIGH      High-priority ACCEPT rules (before packetbl/GeoIP/Block List)
  ISSABEL_BLOCK     Block List DROP rules
  ISSABEL_INPUT     normal INPUT rules (before the final REJECT)
  ISSABEL_FORWARD   normal FORWARD rules
  ISSABEL_OUTPUT    normal OUTPUT rules

Example (commented out in 10-custom.rules.sample):

  *filter
  -A ISSABEL_INPUT -p tcp --dport 8443 -j ACCEPT
  COMMIT

Remember that a rule appended to ISSABEL_INPUT by a custom file is placed
before the rules managed from the web interface, because custom files are
applied first.
